{
  "title": "Paginate list_client_logs and compute content_length in-DB",
  "description": "server/src/api/client_logs/list.rs loads every one of the \
caller's client_log_uploads rows in full (content up to 2MB each, unbounded \
row count) just to compute content_length = row.content.len() in Rust. That is \
an unbounded amount of log payload pulled into memory on every list call.\n\
\n\
Fix: add limit/offset (or cursor) pagination to the endpoint, and compute \
content_length in the database instead of materializing content client-side in \
the handler. Since raw SQL is off-limits, wrap Postgres's octet_length in a \
Diesel define_sql_function! declaration and select it alongside the other \
columns instead of selecting the content column at all.\n\
\n\
Server-side only; update the OpenAPI response/query params and the generated \
clients as needed.",
  "status": "open",
  "priority": 3,
  "type": "task",
  "labels": [
    "api",
    "performance",
  ],
